================================================================
 IPA core-clock power-save — board DTS variant (Asus X00TD)
================================================================

 Same effect as dts/sdm636-asus-x00td-ipa-powersave.dtso, but as a direct
 patch to the board DTS — for boot chains that cannot apply DT overlays.

 Drops the static 200 MHz IPA core_clk pin (assigned-clocks /
 assigned-clock-rates) so the driver's dynamic clock scaling owns the rate.
 Pairs with patches/sdm660-ipa-port-6.19-powersave.patch — apply that one
 first (it enables enable_clock_scaling and retunes the bandwidth
 thresholds). With only this DTS change and the stock driver the IPA clock
 would fall to the RPM boot default (~75 MHz); do not apply it alone.

 APPLY (in your 6.19 kernel tree, after the 4.19 baseline overlay that
 provides this DTS):
   patch -p1 < patches/sdm660-ipa-port-6.19-powersave.patch
   patch -p1 < patches/sdm636-asus-x00td-ipa-powersave-dts.patch

 Clocks and interconnects are untouched; only the assigned-clock* pin goes.

 Generated: 2026-06-04
================================================================

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm636-asus-x00td.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm636-asus-x00td.dts
@@ -732,9 +732,14 @@
 			 <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_AGGR2_NOC_CLK>;
 		clock-names = "core_clk", "smmu_clk";
 
-        /* Force RPM clock vote at probe time regardless of driver bugs */
-        assigned-clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_IPA_CLK>;
-        assigned-clock-rates = <200000000>;       /* 200 MHz turbo */
+		/* Power-save: the IPA core_clk rate is owned by the driver's
+		 * dynamic clock scaling — see sdm660-ipa-port-6.19-powersave.patch.
+		 * No static assigned-clock* pin: the clock gates off when idle and
+		 * scales SVS(75)/NOMINAL(150)/TURBO(200) MHz under the ipa_rm votes.
+		 * If you did NOT apply that patch, keep the vendor pin instead:
+		 *     assigned-clocks      = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_IPA_CLK>;
+		 *     assigned-clock-rates = <200000000>;
+		 */
 
 		/* SMMU stream IDs for the IPA core itself */
 		iommus = <&anoc2_smmu 0x19C0>,
